.TH DANBY-LANCHESTER 1
.SH NAME
danby-lanchester \- Lanchester square-law combat model
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/lanchester
.SH MODEL
A'=-bB; B'=-aA.
.PP
A and B are opposing force strengths; a is A's effectiveness against B and b
is B's effectiveness against A.  The square-law invariant aA^2-bB^2 is
constant until one force reaches zero.  This provides a quantitative model
separate from the graphical
.B battlelines
game.
.SH DISPLAY
Two histories and editable current-strength bars show attrition and the
survivor.  Changing effectiveness exposes why initial numerical superiority
and effectiveness enter quadratically.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag either force bar.  Tracks set the two effectiveness coefficients.  Space
pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH NUMERICS
The differential invariant is checked analytically by
.B temple/danbytest.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/plugin/lanchester.b
.br
.B /appl/danby/lanchester.b
.SH SEE ALSO
